.TH DR-STEIN 1 2026-11-20 "Dr Stein" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dr-stein \- disk and disk-image multitool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dr-stein
.RI [ image ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dr-stein
starts Dr Stein, a graphical tool that shows how a disk or a disk image is
laid out (partition tables, LUKS containers, LVM volumes, file systems),
browses and previews the files inside without mounting them, images disks
and partitions and restores them, edits and repairs partition tables, and
runs surface scans and fake-flash capacity tests.
.PP
Everything opens read-only; writes need an explicit confirmation.
Image files need no privileges. Real disks need administrator rights, which
the app asks for through
.BR pkexec (1)
when it is relaunched from its top bar.
.PP
Each
.I image
named on the command line is added to the sidebar and the last one is
opened. The app reads raw and split raw images, qcow2, VHD, VHDX, VMDK, VDI,
E01, DMG and its own .stein images.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DRSTEIN_VIEW
The view to start on:
.BR topology ", " hex ", " browse ", " image ", " profiles ", " tools " or " partitions .
.TP
.B DRSTEIN_SCHEME
.BR dark " or " light
for this run.
.TP
.B DRSTEIN_PREVIEW
.BR 0 " or " 1 :
file previews in Browse off or on for this run; the stored setting is left
alone.
.TP
.BR DRSTEIN_SCREENSHOT ", " DRSTEIN_DELAY ", " DRSTEIN_SCRIPT
Scripted runs: save the window as a PNG file after DRSTEIN_DELAY milliseconds
(2500 by default) and quit; evaluate JavaScript in the main window one second
after the start.
.PP
Dr Stein carries its own Qt in
.IR /opt/dr-stein .
It ignores
.BR QT_PLUGIN_PATH ", " QML_IMPORT_PATH " and " QML2_IMPORT_PATH ,
which point at another Qt, and it runs on X11 (on Wayland through XWayland)
whatever
.B QT_QPA_PLATFORM
asks for.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dr_stein/
Settings and the list of recent images; by default the profiles folder is
under it as well.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/dr-stein/copyright
The licences of Dr Stein and of the Qt it carries.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
https://github.com/streamx3/dr_stein
